A||||13||elfiero||"BAGGING" a fiero||||6||
Z||000000||elfiero||07-27-2001||09:24 AM|||| Has anyone here put air bags in their fiero<BR>yet? I'm think'in I might have to try it.the<BR>only problem I'm working on is where to put<BR>the tanks and compressors.also,the system<BR>should have two batteries-there isn't hardly<BR>room for one!any ideas? lets put our heads<BR>togther!!!!||||reg||6
Z||000001||Wolfhound||07-27-2001||09:33 AM||||Tanks and compressor? Air bags use solid rocket propellant, Made by Morton-Thycol.<BR>I personally would not like to hemmed up in a Fiero with an air bag.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Philphine||07-27-2001||09:45 AM||||i've seen those struts that have air bags built into them. maybe one might be adaptable to the rear. the 16 vaulve black/yellow fiero that was in hotrod mag long ago had firebird front struts transfered to the rear. that may be a good place to start. don't know about the front.<P>if they work like air shocks you don't really need the tank and compressor. they're just for convienience. or (i think. i'm kinda guessing and going by stuff i've read only a little about) just use a small compressor. i think the tank is to store air from an on board compressor to make the bags fill quicker, or even hop if you have those "fast bags". i have no idea what the extra battery is for, unless you want to play with it with the car off.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Joe Torma||07-27-2001||10:08 AM||||Yeah,  you'll have to look for the strut bags.  As for the fronts...air shocks won't cut it for hopping.  You don't have to have another battery...that's another 50lbs for the air to have to raise.  Get a air compressor and a big tank(may take forever to fill with a small compressor).  stick em in the trunk.  the bigger the line and orifices of the bags/shocks, the faster you'll go up.  1/2 is hyraulics-like fast!  My brother has tried all of this in his Camaro.  Then he realized...his car was meant to just go fast and ripped it all out.<P>Joe<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 07-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||07-27-2001||10:31 AM||||For the bags themselves, i dont know what you might get. Caddy and Lincolns have air suspensions avail that use a small on board air compressor you might use. They dont have any tank. They just use the compressor to lift it and bleed it off to lower it. Prob pretty cheap in a junkyard. Another way to go would be coil overs, not that expensive and there manually adustable up or down a few inches. There already available for Fieros.||||reg||1
Z||000005||elfiero||07-27-2001||10:50 AM||||I already found a place to get the bags,its<BR>a ricer website called the hack-shack.com<BR>they sell all sorts of bags.I figure I'll<BR>cut out the front susp.stops to fit the fronts and use the ones that fit over the<BR>sturts in the rear.I know you need tanks and<BR>large dia. lines for fast response thats why<BR>I think its important to find a place for them.If I can accomplish this,THEN I'll put<BR>a chinspoiler on my car.My car is already<BR>lowered 2 3/4" so a spoiler would last about<BR>5 minutes or 5 miles.anyway,anymore ideas is<BR>appreciated.||||reg||6
Z||000006||Joe Torma||07-27-2001||12:06 PM||||I don't know about your experience with the bags, but mine is that they float around quite a bit in the lower part of the ride height...be careful with that air dam!||||reg||1
