Z||000009||crystalgeek||07-27-2001||08:41 PM||||Hello 87FieroGTx,<BR>I believe that in this case, the "airbags" are for the vehicles suspension, not for the steering wheel or glovebox to protect the passengers.<BR>Airbags are placed in the suspension to control the height of the vehicle.  If you get enough air in the bags fast enough, you get the car to hop around.  Lots of fun if you like whiplash ;O).<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Thanks,<BR>Alex O<BR>"I'd give my right arm to be ambidextrous"||||reg||1
Z||000010||artherd||07-27-2001||08:59 PM||||Uh, WHAT?!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000011||862M4inCA||07-27-2001||09:47 PM||||Not to sound rude or anything but, a Fiero that hops around like a slammed caddy or mini-truck.....sounds like one could find a much better use for the money. Stock Fieros already look good, no need to make them "bounce" like mexican jumping beans. ||||reg||1
Z||000012||rockcrawl||07-27-2001||10:01 PM||||Wouldn't it be great to have a normal ride height for cruising, and then when you park, drop the sucker down to the pavement. I've been thinking a lot about air bag suspension for Fieros too. The bottom of the trunk seems like a great place for the compressor and a small tank. Cadillac compressors are littering the junk yards. I just recently started seeing the air-over struts for the ricers. I wonder if that type of system would be adaptable to the Fiero rear stuts. The front would be a piece of cake, just gotta size the bags properly. <BR>I see AirLift is now selling York style A/C compressors for use with their suspension systems. If your Fiero has an A/C compressor that's not being used for A/C, that would be a perfect pump. I've used A/C compressors on several trucks for filling tires and powering air tools, they are very quick and contrary to popular belief they last very long. You just gotta keep oil in them.<P>My major concern is how it will ride. I don't want to go bouncing down the road. I guess it can't be so bad, the Cadillac has air struts on the rear to adjust height to compensate for loads. The only difference is that the caddy also has a standard coil spring. The air-over struts don't use a spring at all.||||reg||14
Z||000013||West Coast Fiero||07-28-2001||03:09 PM||||from experience, get an oppropriately matched compressor for the tank, if the tank is to large you WILL burn out the compressor from being over-run||||reg||1
